This product's design draws on lessons from the community plugin
dsh-email-notify <https://github.com/MCviseron/dsh-email-notify>
(Apache License 2.0, Copyright (c) MCviseron), in particular:

  - declaring the auth code as a schemastery field with `.role('secret')` so the
    settings service redacts it before it reaches the browser;
  - letting the profile entry Config be the settings namespace instead of
    registering a second one;
  - keeping SMTP credentials out of logs, error messages and API responses.

No source code was copied from that project: this plugin is an independent,
smaller implementation written for its own requirements, and it does not ship
any of dsh-email-notify's notification triggers, templates or client bundle.
